    markdown: "# GrayBag Refund Policy\n\n**Notice version 2** · Effective 2026-08-11\n\n## Change log\n\n### Version 2 — 2026-08-11\n\n| # | Section | Change | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Contact Us | `info@graybag.in` → **`info@graybag.com`** | A typo in the baseline, confirmed by Andy on 2026-08-11. `graybag.com` is the correct email domain. Recorded as a correction rather than a decision — the lawyer's intent was the working address, and a published contact that bounces is worse than no contact at all |\n\n**Not changed, and deliberately so:** the \"5–7 business days\" refund timing. `E06-33` records\nthat the figure in the *app's* order-detail screen was invented and needs to come from\nRazorpay's actual settlement behaviour. This document is the lawyer's published commitment and\nis not ours to quietly re-time; if the real figure differs, that is a new notice version and a\nconversation with the lawyer, not an edit.\n\n---\n\nAt GrayBag, we are committed to delivering a reliable and parent-friendly experience. We\nunderstand the importance of timely and nutritious meals for children, and we strive to\nmaintain the highest standards of service.\n\n## Order Cancellations by GrayBag\n\nOccasionally, we may need to cancel an order due to unforeseen circumstances, such as:\n\n- Unavailability of selected item(s)\n- Delivery constraints (e.g., school closures, access restrictions)\n- Technical or operational issues\n\nIf GrayBag cancels your order, a full refund will be issued to the original method of payment\nwithin 5–7 business days.\n\n## Refund Eligibility\n\n- Refunds are only processed for orders cancelled by GrayBag.\n- In the event of partial fulfillment (e.g., one item unavailable), a proportional refund may\n  be issued.\n- If an issue arises after delivery, customers must raise a complaint within 24 hours via the\n  app or support email.\n\n## General Terms\n\n- Refund timelines may vary based on your bank or payment provider.\n- GrayBag reserves the right to refuse refund claims in cases of suspected misuse, fraud, or\n  repeated complaints not supported by evidence.\n- Refund decisions are made at the sole discretion of GrayBag and are considered final.\n\n## Dispute Resolution\n\nIn the unlikely event of a dispute, we encourage you to contact us first. Any disputes arising\nout of this policy shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts in SAS Nagar\n(Mohali), India.\n\n## Contact Us\n\nFor questions or concerns, please reach out to us at info@graybag.com or through the in-app\nhelp section.\n",
